 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "Rome conquered half the known world, and its secret weapon wasn't the sword.",
   "start": 0.35,
   "end": 3.753,
   "para": 0
  },
  {
   "text": "It was the shovel.",
   "start": 4.033,
   "end": 4.747,
   "para": 0
  },
  {
   "text": "It's around one hundred B C.",
   "start": 5.297,
   "end": 6.829,
   "para": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "Rome is a city of farmers on seven hills, surrounded by neighbours who would really like to burn it down.",
   "start": 7.109,
   "end": 11.376,
   "para": 1
  },
  {
   "text": "So every Roman soldier carries his own gear on his back.",
   "start": 11.926,
   "end": 14.256,
   "para": 2
  },
  {
   "text": "Armour, food, a cooking pot and a shovel.",
   "start": 14.536,
   "end": 16.564,
   "para": 2
  },
  {
   "text": "Thirty kilos of it.",
   "start": 16.844,
   "end": 17.673,
   "para": 2
  },
  {
   "text": "People called them Marius's mules.",
   "start": 17.953,
   "end": 19.421,
   "para": 2
  },
  {
   "text": "At the end of every day's march, they don't just pitch tents.",
   "start": 19.971,
   "end": 22.821,
   "para": 3
  },
  {
   "text": "They dig a ditch, pile up a wall, and build a whole fortified camp.",
   "start": 23.101,
   "end": 26.188,
   "para": 3
  },
  {
   "text": "Every single night.",
   "start": 26.468,
   "end": 27.278,
   "para": 3
  },
  {
   "text": "Behind the army come the roads.",
   "start": 27.828,
   "end": 29.074,
   "para": 4
  },
  {
   "text": "Dead straight, layer on layer of stone, gravel and sand.",
   "start": 29.354,
   "end": 32.102,
   "para": 4
  },
  {
   "text": "Eventually more than eighty thousand kilometres of them.",
   "start": 32.382,
   "end": 34.492,
   "para": 4
  },
  {
   "text": "An army that once took a month to arrive now shows up in a week.",
   "start": 35.042,
   "end": 37.576,
   "para": 5
  },
  {
   "text": "Then, in fifty five B C, Julius Caesar wants to cross the Rhine to scare the tribes on the other side.",
   "start": 38.126,
   "end": 42.899,
   "para": 6
  },
  {
   "text": "There are no boats.",
   "start": 43.179,
   "end": 43.936,
   "para": 6
  },
  {
   "text": "So his men build a wooden bridge across the whole river.",
   "start": 44.216,
   "end": 46.432,
   "para": 6
  },
  {
   "text": "In ten days.",
   "start": 46.712,
   "end": 47.317,
   "para": 6
  },
  {
   "text": "Luckily, the tribes were very impressed.",
   "start": 47.867,
   "end": 49.728,
   "para": 7
  },
  {
   "text": "Unluckily for the bridge, Caesar walked back eighteen days later and had it torn down.",
   "start": 50.008,
   "end": 53.78,
   "para": 7
  },
  {
   "text": "Here's the real trick.",
   "start": 54.33,
   "end": 55.199,
   "para": 8
  },
  {
   "text": "An empire works like a pizza chain.",
   "start": 55.479,
   "end": 57.136,
   "para": 8
  },
  {
   "text": "Winning a town is opening a new branch.",
   "start": 57.416,
   "end": 58.935,
   "para": 8
  },
  {
   "text": "Keeping it means the delivery has to arrive hot.",
   "start": 59.215,
   "end": 61.117,
   "para": 8
  },
  {
   "text": "Roads were Rome's delivery network.",
   "start": 61.397,
   "end": 62.882,
   "para": 8
  },
  {
   "text": "Soldiers, letters, taxes and grain, all moving fast.",
   "start": 63.162,
   "end": 66.092,
   "para": 8
  },
  {
   "text": "And Rome didn't keep the people it beat as enemies.",
   "start": 66.642,
   "end": 68.848,
   "para": 9
  },
  {
   "text": "It slowly made them Roman.",
   "start": 69.128,
   "end": 70.323,
   "para": 9
  },
  {
   "text": "Their sons joined the legions, picked up shovels, and built the next road.",
   "start": 70.603,
   "end": 74.06,
   "para": 9
  },
  {
   "text": "By two twelve A D, almost every free person in the empire was a citizen.",
   "start": 74.34,
   "end": 77.539,
   "para": 9
  },
  {
   "text": "At its peak the empire ran from Scotland to Iraq, with around sixty million people.",
   "start": 78.089,
   "end": 81.959,
   "para": 10
  },
  {
   "text": "And in the middle of Rome stood a golden milestone, where every road began.",
   "start": 82.239,
   "end": 85.359,
   "para": 10
  },
  {
   "text": "All roads really did lead to Rome.",
   "start": 85.909,
   "end": 87.339,
   "para": 11
  },
  {
   "text": "Which was great, right up until four ten A D, when an army of Goths followed one straight to the gate.",
   "start": 87.619,
   "end": 92.086,
   "para": 11
  }
 ]
}